    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Powerhouse document model testing follows a structured pattern using Vitest:\n\n1. **Create a document**: `utils.createDocument()` or `utils.createDocument({ global: { items: [mockItem] } })` with initial state\n2. **Generate typed mocks**: `generateMock(AddTodoItemInputSchema())` creates objects with random values matching the schema\n3. **Apply operations**: `const updated = reducer(document, addTodoItem(input))`\n4. **Validate**: `expect(isTodoListDocument(updated)).toBe(true)` for schema validation\n5. **Assert state**: Check `updated.state.global.items` for correct data\n6. **Assert operations**: Check `updated.operations.global[0].action.type` for correct operation recording\n\nKey testing utilities come from the generated code:\n- `reducer` - The document reducer function\n- `utils.createDocument()` - Creates empty or pre-populated documents\n- `isTodoListDocument()` - Schema validation predicate\n- `generateMock()` from `document-model` (re-exported via `@powerhousedao/shared/document-model`) - Schema-aware mock generation\n- `*Schema()` functions - Schema definitions for mock generation\n\nBest practice: Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert). Test immutability, edge cases, and cover both state changes and operation recording.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._\n\n## Correction at v6.2.2-dev.74\nThe import moved: `generateMock` is now imported from **`document-model/mock`**, its own package export \u2014 not from `@powerhousedao/codegen` and not from the `document-model` root. All three Academy test tutorials were corrected to that subpath. The surrounding pattern (`utils.createDocument()`, schema-derived mocks, asserting on state, reading reducer errors off the operation) is unchanged.\n",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-02T22:26:50.567Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-02T22:26:50.567Z"
    }
